{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.zero_candidate_descent","record":{"id":"support.zero_candidate_descent","kind":"claim","label":"The zero coefficient is not minimizing","status":"unverified","source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","locator":"Long reasoning record #zero-coefficient-example","statement":"For the admissible zero coefficient in pure zero-field SK, q0(t)=2 arcsin(t)/pi and D+P(0)[1]=1/4-1/pi<0. Thus empty Stieltjes support cannot occur at a minimizer. The calculation does not inherit minimizer moment identities.","assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_admissible"],"citation_ids":["authored_r8_support_zero_candidate_descent"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_deductions_review_20261026"],"boundary":"Ordinary authored deduction checked against retained mathematical inputs; no new Lean declaration, elaborated dependency, cross-model transport, Comparator acceptance or independent proof certification is asserted."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.zero_candidate_descent","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/2f85413164f06365ea0d825befee447650da71d54080d5dd65e78a708891c560","roles":["mapped_claim"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/9dd5536bc567fc55efaa864733bf89747cea0268a8a3865dec51ddd8e2a235dd","roles":["mapped_claim"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/passages/gaussian-sanity-check","anchor":"gaussian-sanity-check","mapping_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"},{"stage":"expository","passage_ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/passages/zero-candidate","anchor":"zero-candidate","mapping_ref":"sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/passages/gaussian-sanity-check","anchor":"gaussian-sanity-check","mapping_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\n\n<a id=\"zero-coefficient-example\"></a>\n\n### 10.3 The zero coefficient\n\nThe admissible coefficient $\\gamma_0=0$ makes the use of minimality in\nthe normalization step explicit. Its diffusion is $X_t=B_t$, and the\n[zero-coefficient heat formula][fs-reg] gives\n\n$$\nu_0(t,x)=2F_{\\mathrm G}\\!\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-t}}\\right)-1,\n\\qquad\na_0(t,x)=\\sqrt{\\frac2\\pi}\\frac{e^{-x^2/(2(1-t))}}{\\sqrt{1-t}}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbb E e^{-\\lambda B_t^2}=(1+2\\lambda t)^{-1/2}$,\n\n$$\n\\mathbb E a_0(t,B_t)=\\sqrt{\\frac2\\pi},\\qquad\n\\mathbb E a_0(t,B_t)^2=\\frac2{\\pi\\sqrt{1-t^2}},\\qquad\nq_0(t)=\\frac2\\pi\\arcsin t.\n$$\n\nThe last identity follows by integrating $q_0'=\\mathbb E a_0^2$\nfrom $q_0(0)=0$. This heat and late-step variation argument is the\nzero-field specialization of [Chen, Handschy and Lerman, Theorem 6\nand its proof, arXiv:1609.04368v4, pp. 13–16](https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.04368v4).\nStrict convexity of $\\arcsin$ gives $q_0(t)<t$\nfor $0<t<1$. Thus $G_0(s)=\\int_s^1(q_0(t)-t)\\,dt<0$ for\nevery $s<1$. Inserting an atom at $s$ is admissible, and its\n[first variation][fs-var] is $G_0(s)/2<0$. In particular, the derivative for inserting\nmass at zero is $1/4-1/\\pi<0$. Hence this coefficient does not\nminimize.\n\nHere the Euler scheme is exact: $Y_j=B_{t_j}$ under the Brownian\ncoupling. Nevertheless its normalizers are\n\n$$\nc_j=\\sqrt{\\frac\\pi2}\\,(1-t_{j-1}^2)^{1/4},\n$$\n\nso they approximate this nonconstant function of time, rather than\nconverging uniformly to one. Already $c_1=\\sqrt{\\pi/2}$ for every\nmesh. The directions $g_j$ remain orthonormal by construction and the\nrounding still preserves conditional means; the missing input to the\nvalue limit is the minimizing identity $\\mathbb E a(t,X_t)^2=1$.\n\nThe terminal spin also survives:\n$U_1=\\operatorname{sgn}(B_1)$ almost surely. But its correlation is\n\n$$\n\\mathbb E[U_1B_1]=\\sqrt{\\frac2\\pi}=\\mathcal P(\\gamma_0),\n$$\n\nthe value of this nonminimizing candidate. The negative first variation\nproves that this value is strictly above $P_*$. Admissibility, exact\nEuler sampling, and a spin-valued terminal martingale therefore do not\nsupply the minimizing normalization or identify the ground-state value.\n","span":{"start_byte":192326,"end_byte":194473,"start_line":4117,"end_line":4175},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=gaussian-sanity-check","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=gaussian-sanity-check"},{"stage":"expository","passage_ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/passages/zero-candidate","anchor":"zero-candidate","mapping_ref":"sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\n\\Needspace{11\\baselineskip}\n\n### 7.1 Why the zero candidate does not minimise\n\nReturn to the Gaussian value and slope from Section 3. With $\\gamma=0$,\nthe state is $B_t$. Differentiating the slope once more gives\n\n$$\nX_t=B_t,\\qquad\nu_0(t,x)=2F_{\\mathrm G}\\!\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-t}}\\right)-1,\n\\qquad\na_0(t,x)=\\sqrt{\\frac2{\\pi(1-t)}}e^{-x^2/(2(1-t))}.\n$$\n\nA Gaussian integral gives\n$\\mathbb E e^{-B_t^2/(1-t)}=\\sqrt{(1-t)/(1+t)}$. Substituting\ninto $q_0'=\\mathbb E[a_0(t,B_t)^2]$ and integrating from zero yields\n\n$$\nq_0'(t)=\\frac2{\\pi\\sqrt{1-t^2}},\\qquad\nq_0(t)=\\frac2\\pi\\arcsin t.\n$$\n\nThis recovers the half-time value $1/3$. It also shows that\n$q_0(t)\\to1$ while $q_0'(t)\\to\\infty$: convergence of a function\nat one does not bound its derivative there.\nThe constant direction $\\eta=1$ is admissible and adds an atom at zero.\nIts cost is\n\n$$\nD\\mathcal P(0)[1]\n=\\frac12\\int_0^1\\left(\\frac2\\pi\\arcsin t-t\\right)dt\n=\\frac14-\\frac1\\pi<0.\n$$\n\nSo a small positive constant coefficient improves the zero candidate.\nThis calculation uses the heat and variation formulas, not a minimiser\nhypothesis; see also [Chen–Handschy–Lerman, proof of Theorem 6][chl-optimality].\n","span":{"start_byte":45248,"end_byte":46415,"start_line":1070,"end_line":1108},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/expository?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=expository&passage=zero-candidate","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=expository&passage=zero-candidate"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=support.zero_candidate_descent&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=support.zero_candidate_descent&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=support.zero_candidate_descent&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=support.zero_candidate_descent&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"field:5331a3f0ad0ade136894af4add9fb8fd4d1733f1a3e96130e2af79944a67b45e","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.zero_candidate_descent","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.paper_admissible","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.zero_candidate_descent","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.zero_candidate_descent%22%2C%22support.diffusion%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.zero_candidate_descent","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.diffusion","kind":"supports","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","derived":false,"record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.zero_candidate_descent%22%2C%22support.diffusion%22%2C%22supports%22%5D"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.zero_candidate_descent%22%2C%22support.first_variation%22%2C%22su